    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be a fixed point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be a moving point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> be the mid-point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and the perpendicular bisector of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> meets the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The locus of the mid-point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MC</mi></math> is</p>"
